exports[`makeFixUnit — disk is the source of truth > uses regression repair prompt with rejected diff, exact findings, and gate output 1`] = `
"# Regression repair task

A previous edit cleared its finding but the safety gate rejected it. Keep that fix and repair the
rejection. State its root cause in one sentence (read the history), make the minimal edit, then
confirm each finding is gone with no new tsc error.

The rejected attempt is still on disk — repair it:
<file_contents>
### src/a.ts

\`\`\`
if (cond) {
  doWork();
}

\`\`\`
</file_contents>

Findings the fix must still resolve:
<findings>
\`\`\`json
[
  {
    "file": "src/a.ts",
    "range": {
      "startLine": 1,
      "startCol": 0,
      "endLine": 1,
      "endCol": 10
    },
    "tool": "sonarjs",
    "rule": "no-identical-expressions",
    "category": "bug",
    "severity": "error",
    "message": "Identical sub-expressions"
  }
]
\`\`\`
</findings>

<editable_files>
- src/a.ts
</editable_files>

Every rejected attempt so far (oldest first) with its diff, any new findings, and the gate
output — address their shared root cause, don't re-walk them:
<attempt_history>
### Attempt 1 (rejected)

<rejected_diff>
\`\`\`diff
-const x = a == b;
+if (cond) {
+  doWork();
+}
\`\`\`
</rejected_diff>

New findings it introduced:
<new_findings>
\`\`\`json
[
  {
    "file": "src/a.ts",
    "range": {
      "startLine": 2,
      "startCol": 0,
      "endLine": 2,
      "endCol": 10
    },
    "tool": "sonarjs",
    "rule": "cognitive-complexity",
    "category": "bug",
    "severity": "error",
    "message": "Function has too much cognitive complexity"
  }
]
\`\`\`
</new_findings>

Gate output:
<gate_output>
\`\`\`text
Reason: regression
Fix introduced new finding(s): src/a.ts:2 cognitive-complexity
\`\`\`
</gate_output>
</attempt_history>

Done when the original findings stay fixed and the failure no longer reproduces:
<verification_targets>
- src/a.ts
</verification_targets>"
`;
